#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:62
msgid "2.1 Frequency Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:64
msgid ""
"The ``out_altvoltage0_frequency`` attribute controls the RF output frequency "
"with sub-Hz precision. The driver automatically selects between integer-N "
"and fractional-N modes to achieve the requested frequency with the best "
"possible phase noise performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:69
msgid "**Supported ranges:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:71
msgid "**ADF41510**: 1,000,000,000 Hz to 10,000,000,000 Hz (1 GHz to 10 GHz)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:72
msgid "**ADF41513**: 1,000,000,000 Hz to 26,500,000,000 Hz (1 GHz to 26.5 GHz)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:74
msgid ""
"The frequency is specified in Hz, for sub-Hz precision use decimal notation. "
"For example, 12.102 GHz would be written as \"12102000000.000000\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:78
msgid "2.2 Frequency Resolution Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:80
msgid ""
"The ``out_altvoltage0_frequency_resolution`` attribute controls the target "
"frequency resolution that the driver attempts to achieve. This affects the "
"choice between integer-N and fractional-N modes, including fixed modulus (25-"
"bit) and variable modulus (49-bit) fractional-N modes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:85
msgid "**Integer-N**: Resolution = :math:`f_{PFD}` (same as PFD frequency)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:86
msgid ""
"**Fixed modulus**: Resolution = :math:`f_{PFD} / 2^{25}` (~3 Hz with 100 MHz "
"PFD)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:87
msgid ""
"**Variable modulus**: Resolution = :math:`f_{PFD} / 2^{49}` (µHz resolution "
"possible)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:89
msgid "Default resolution is 1 Hz (1,000,000 µHz)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:92
msgid "2.3 Phase adjustment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:94
msgid ""
"The ``out_altvoltage0_phase`` attribute allows adjustment of the output "
"phase in radians. Setting this attribute enables phase adjustment. It can be "
"set from 0 to :math:`2\\pi` radians. Reading this attribute returns the "
"current phase offset of the output signal. To create a consistent phase "
"relationship with the reference signal, the phase resync feature needs to be "
"enabled by setting a non-zero value to the ``adi,phase-resync-period-ns`` "
"device property, which triggers a phase resynchronization after locking is "
"achieved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:103
msgid "3. Operating modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:106
msgid "3.1 Integer-N Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:108
msgid ""
"When the requested frequency can be achieved as an integer multiple of the "
"PFD frequency (within the specified resolution tolerance), the driver "
"automatically selects integer-N mode for optimal phase noise performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:112
msgid "In integer-N mode:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:114
msgid "Phase noise: -235 dBc/Hz normalized floor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:115
msgid "Frequency resolution: :math:`f_{PFD}` (same as PFD frequency)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:116
msgid "Maximum PFD frequency: 250 MHz"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:117
msgid "Bleed current: Disabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:120
msgid "3.2 Fractional-N Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:122
msgid ""
"When sub-integer frequency steps are required, the driver automatically "
"selects fractional-N mode using either fixed or variable modulus."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:125
msgid "**Fixed Modulus (25-bit)**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/adf41513.rst:127
